---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Base title="About" description="What DevStack is and how each article is written.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="plain">
      <h1>About DevStack</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          DevStack is a personal reading library. Each book becomes one long article that follows
          the author's argument from the first chapter to the last, with enough detail that you can
          answer specific questions about any chapter without opening the book.
        </p>

        <h2>What is in an article</h2>
        <p>Every article is built the same way, so you always know where to look.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>An overview: what the book is, its thesis, and its shape in one pass.</li>
          <li>
            Chapter summaries, one subheading per chapter in the book's own order. Each is a
            detailed account of what happens or what is argued, with the names, numbers, and
            examples that make it distinct.
          </li>
          <li>A "Key takeaway" closing every chapter, so the point survives the detail.</li>
          <li>Themes and analysis: the through-line, where the book is strong, and where it is thin.</li>
          <li>Recall questions at the end. Try them before you open the answers.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Claims are attributed to the author. Commentary is kept separate and labeled, so you
          always know whose view you are reading.
        </p>

        <h2>How to read one</h2>
        <p>
          Read the overview first. Then take the chapters in order, or jump to one from the
          contents list. Wait a day, then answer the recall questions from memory and open only
          the answers you missed.
        </p>

        <h2 id="add-a-book">How books are added</h2>
        <p>
          Books are added through a chat agent that works on this site's repository. The steps are
          the same each time:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>Attach the PDF or EPUB and ask the agent to ingest it.</li>
          <li>The agent extracts the text, splits it by chapter, and checks that nothing was lost.</li>
          <li>It writes the article and adds the book's page, topic, and navigation entries.</li>
          <li>A validator confirms every chapter is covered and every quote is short.</li>
          <li>The agent publishes the site and reports what changed.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Want to follow along? <a href={url('/rss.xml')}>Subscribe by RSS</a>, or
          <a href={url('/library/')}>browse the library</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
